# Pre-deploy preview (Cloudflare tunnel)

Before recommending or running a **production deploy**, preview on a **Cloudflare tunnel hostname** — not `localhost` alone and not production `assistedly.ai`.

## Tunnel hostnames (same connector token)

| URL | Local bridge port | Use when |
|-----|-------------------|----------|
| **https://agent1.assistedly.ai/** | 3001 | Default preview |
| **https://agent2.assistedly.ai/** | 3002 | agent1 busy or port conflict on 3001 |
| **https://agent3.assistedly.ai/** | 3003 | agent1/agent2 both busy |
| **https://dev.assistedly.ai/** | 3010 direct | Next dev on 3010 (no bridge); still needs `npm run tunnel:dev` |

Set **`DEV_PUBLIC_URL`** in **`.env.local`** to switch (e.g. `DEV_PUBLIC_URL=https://agent3.assistedly.ai`).

## Workflow (on your Mac, in this Cursor workspace)

1. `npm run dev` (port scan from **3010**; note printed port).
2. **`ASSISTEDLY_TUNNEL_TOKEN`** in **`.env.local`** (see `.env.example`).
3. If tunnel returns **1033** / **502**, stop origin connector:
   `ssh -i ~/.ssh/7-5-25kuroit opencode@75.127.14.185 'sudo systemctl stop cloudflared'`
4. `npm run tunnel:dev` (auto-clears stale bridge ports 3001–3005; manual: `npm run tunnel:kill-bridges`).
5. Restart **`npm run dev`** after **API/server** file changes (`pages/api/`, `lib/*` used by API).

Restore origin when done:  
`ssh -i ~/.ssh/7-5-25kuroit opencode@75.127.14.185 'sudo systemctl start cloudflared'`

## Agent expectations (required)

- After **every reviewable code update**, end the reply with a **Cloudflare tunnel preview line** (full URL with trailing slash), e.g.  
  **Cloudflare tunnel preview: https://agent1.assistedly.ai/**
- If the user should use agent2/agent3, say so and print **https://agent2.assistedly.ai/** or **https://agent3.assistedly.ai/** instead.
- Run `node scripts/print-test-url.js` when confirming a build or handing off for QA.
- Do **not** use production `https://assistedly.ai/` as the first preview link for unmerged work.
